abstract = {A bound is obtained for the error incurred when derivatives are found in terms of differences. The method depends on the use of an auxiliary function, and it is shown that by appropriately choosing the auxiliary function one may considerably improve the estimate of the error, especially in the neighbourhood of a singularity. The result, in addition, provides an alternative form for the remainder term in interpolation formulae, and it can also be regarded as an extension of Cauchy's generalised mean-value theorem.},
